# Golf Solutions (GS) — Consumer Web

## What this repo is

Frontend for **Golf Solutions Jakarta**: TrackMan fitting, coaching, and pro shop across two locations. Phase 1 consumer surface only — landing through purchase, booking, and account.

PRD companion: Staff Console (PRD 2) and fitter tools (PRD 3) are **out of scope** for `apps/web`.

## Role boundary

- This repo / your work: **frontend only**
- Backend (auth sessions, stock holds, payment jobs, WhatsApp templates, Biteship, gateway): **separate team**
- Do **not** put staff/admin UI inside `apps/web`. When PRD 2 starts, add `apps/staff`

## Monorepo layout

- `apps/web` — consumer (landing + ecommerce + account/booking)
- `apps/staff` — later only
- `packages/contracts` — Zod DTOs shared with BE shape
- `packages/format` — Rp, dates, phone
- `packages/tokens` — design tokens / CSS variables
- `packages/config` — shared tsconfig/eslint/tailwind presets

Personal scratch notes live in `.notes/` (gitignored). Do not commit secrets or private notes there into git.

## Stack (locked)

- **pnpm** workspaces + Turborepo
- Next.js App Router + TypeScript
- Tailwind + **shadcn/ui** as primitives — restyle to Figma; never ship default zinc look
- TanStack Query, React Hook Form + Zod, nuqs, next-intl (EN keys from day one)
- **MSW mocks** until real API exists (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`)
- **PostHog** for PRD §16 analytics events
- Payments: vendor-agnostic DTOs until BE confirms Xendit/Midtrans
- Animation: **`motion`** (Framer Motion) for hero carousel, scroll reveals, section carousels. Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`. Do not use GSAP unless product asks.

## Design fidelity (mandatory) — pixel-perfect

Figma is the **only** source of truth. Implement **exactly** as designed — do not approximate, “close enough,” or invent styles.

Match precisely at the design reference widths — **do not ship desktop-only**:

| Breakpoint | Width | Figma source / behavior |
|---|---|---|
| **Mobile** | **375** | Frame `1:18410` (Mobile) |
| **Tablet** | **~768–1023** (`md`) | Interpolate mobile ↔ desktop |
| **Laptop** | **1024–1279** (`lg`) | Fluid layouts + scaled type — **never** lock fixed 1440px column tracks or 115px hero here |
| **Desktop** | **1280+** (`xl`), pixel lock at **1440** | Landing `1:39` — fixed tracks / full type only from `xl` |

Do **not** apply Figma-1440 fixed grids (e.g. `460px + 836px`) or hero `115px` at `lg` (1024) — that overflows 1024–1400. Use `minmax` / `fr` grids at `lg`, and `xl:` for the desktop lock.

- **Typography** — font family, size, weight, line-height, letter-spacing, text transform, text color/opacity (scale down per mobile Figma; do not leave desktop `text-[58px]` etc. on 375)
- **Spacing** — padding, margin, gap, section rhythm (mobile often `px-5` / `py-10`; desktop `px-10` / larger section padding)
- **Layout** — stack vs grid, horizontal carousels on mobile when Figma shows scrollable rows, widths/heights/max-widths
- **Surfaces** — background color, border, radius, shadow
- **Assets** — images/icons from Figma under `apps/web/public/…`
- **Interactions** — see Micro-interactions below. Hover ≠ default resting state.

Primary typeface: **Oswald** (Light / Regular / Medium / Bold) unless a specific Figma node uses another family (e.g. Helvetica) — then match that node, or **ask** if unclear.

Display headlines often use a slight italic skew (`-skew-x-[5deg]` on the text wrapper) — **only** where Figma does.

When unsure what a node does, which variant to ship, or exact copy/type: **ask the user before implementing**. Do not guess.

## Micro-interactions (mandatory on every interactive UI)

Shared tokens: `apps/web/features/landing/interactions.ts` (`ix.*`). Resting styles stay Figma-accurate; tokens only add hover / focus / active / motion.

Always ship for interactive elements (links, CTAs, cards, chips, icon buttons, tabs, form controls):

- `cursor-pointer`
- Focus-visible outlines
- Hover / press feedback (color, opacity, border, soft shadow as appropriate)
- Image zoom / arrow nudge on card-style targets where Figma implies motion
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (disable transform/zoom animations)
- Do **not** invent hover looks that contradict Figma resting frames (e.g. three-ways stays white until hover → black)

