## Figma MCP — use efficiently (mandatory)

Each `get_design_context` / `get_screenshot` / `get_metadata` costs one tool call. Conserve quota:

- **Section nodes only** — pull the specific section (e.g. camps `1:409`), not the full landing `1:39`, unless structure mapping is truly needed once.
- **Pull once, code offline** — do not re-fetch the same node while iterating CSS/layout.
- **Screenshot only when layout is ambiguous** — skip if design context + existing local assets are enough.
- **Assets stay local** — download to `apps/web/public/landing/` once; never re-download the same file.
- **Reuse prior context** — prefer already-saved metadata, screenshots, and local assets before new MCP calls.
- **Small batches** — at most a few sections per turn; avoid parallel call spam (per-minute cap).
- **Ask the user when unsure** — one confirmation beats speculative re-pulls of variants.
- Do **not** full-page re-audit unless the user asks.
- **Always report MCP usage** — when you call any Figma MCP tool, tell the user in the reply: which tool(s), which node(s), and the call count for that turn (e.g. “3 MCP calls: `get_design_context` on `1:607`, `1:637`, `1:264`”). If you used **0** Figma MCP calls, say so when the task was Figma-related.

## Product rules to respect in UI

- Order countdown from server `paymentExpiresAt` only
- Coaching matrix: regular/by-request × credit/cash; never invent booking statuses
- FittingSpec is versioned — never overwrite in client models
- Phase 1 honesty: no dead links to selectors/trade-in/camps; no fake points/instalments
- Locale: `Rp 24.000.000`, dates like `25 Aug`, 24h times

## When implementing from Figma

Load design-to-code skill, then call `get_design_context` (and screenshot only if needed) **for the target section node** — follow the efficiency rules above. Adapt to this stack; do not paste absolute-position prototypes as production layout. Preserve exact type and spacing values from the design context.
